{
	"title": "Following the sun: a timer that restarts itself evaluates sunAzimuth() and sunElevation() every 5 minutes; onlyOnChange writes the changes only",
	"description": "The pattern of spec/rules.md 4.7 for a rule that follows the sun: the start trigger and the timer's expiry run the same reaction, which restarts the timer and writes whether the sun is on a south-east facade (azimuth 90..200 degrees, more than 10 degrees above the horizon). Berlin, 2026-06-21 from 06:00 CEST for ten hours: the sun is not on the facade at the start, comes onto it in the morning and leaves it in the afternoon, each at the first tick after the crossing.",
	"note": "The expected ticks were computed with the throw-away executable model (spec/blocks.md 13.1 and 13.2) at every tick, cross-checked against the same formulas on the C library and the Astronomical Almanac's low-precision formula; the crossing ticks are not near a threshold within 0.02 degrees.",
